    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28544" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>express in the dual number,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				47.28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be impressed with the sense of a thing's being
				double, see double,</i> etc., <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				7.193
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>make into two,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				432.12
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			): —
				Pass.
			, <i>to be halved,</i> of the moon, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>double,</i> Theo Sm.<i><span class="en">
				p.29
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>in Nic.</u>
				p.60P.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυάζει: φλυαρεῖ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cyr.
			</span></i> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρυάζω</span>); also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυαεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			</div>
